    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1401">

                <pb facs="1131" n="1121" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.7141/12–649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clubb</hi>)<anchor n="52" xml:id="d1401-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-16T19:00:00-05:00">December 16,
                            1949—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>909. Urtel 2227, Dec 6. Position taken Depcirtel Aug 26 still prevails. If tax
                    bills reed they shld be returned with statement ConGen assumes bills sent in
                    error. In returning bills ConGen shld state reason for exception viz., “taxes
                    not payable since a sovereign Govt shld not be taxed on property owned by that
                    Govt and used for Govt purposes”.</p>
                <p>ConGen in its ltrs to Shanghai land admin bureau stated US Govt adheres to
                    internationally accepted principle one country does not tax property of another,
                    US Govt considers itself not liable for payment of taxes.</p>
                <p>Suggest you handle tax problem this basis but keep Dept fully informed.</p>
                <p>Sent Peiping, rptd Shanghai, Nanking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1401-f1" n="52" type="source" xml:id="d1401-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Consul General at Shanghai as No. 2438 and to the Embassy at
                    Nanking as No. 1300.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
